Atlas overlay patch 0022: ui/sidebar-sections
Why: the tab list is grouped under PINNED, TODAY, YESTERDAY and EARLIER headers (reel scene R02, R09;
patches-0 P-07). The sections are visual: the model order stays by position, a dragged tab keeps its
place and its last-active time, empty sections show nothing, a named group keeps its own header and
ends the run before it, and the tab in front is always today's. The grouping and the header painting
are in chrome/browser/ui/atlas/sidebar/sidebar_sections; the containers reserve a band above the
first row of each section in their layout (so the layout manager animates the bands with the rows)
and paint the labels in OnPaint. Only a band inside the container can follow the rows through the
engine's animated layout, so a first-run pref or a policy cannot do this and a lower tier was not
enough. The tab in front asks its container to lay out again when it changes.
A named group's name is a header in small caps with no chip, and while the group is collapsed one
row under it says "N tabs" (a bookmark glyph, the count in the dim colour).
